  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feas Sty Smallholder Sugar Cane Product</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A major development objective of the GOM relates to food security and self suffciency. Closely linked to this is the objective relating to improvement in incomes and welfare of smallholders. The Government&apos;s desire to expand sugar production through smallholders is aimed at achieving the two development objectives, i.e. self-sufficency in sugar, and improvement on the living conditions of smallholders. The purpose of the study is to determine the most suitable and cos-effective strategy of expanding sugar production through smallholders.</narrative>
  </description>
